<p class="headeraddress" style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: right;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">Kimberley A. Komoto</span></p>
<p class="headeraddress" style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: right;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;City Clerk</span></p>
<p class="headeraddress" style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: right;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">220<sup>&nbsp;</sup>4th Avenue South</span></p>
<p class="headeraddress" style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: right;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">Kent, WA 98032</span></p>
<p class="headeraddress" style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: right;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">Fax: 253-856-6725</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: right;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;<strong><span style="text-transform: uppercase;">PHONE:&nbsp; 253-856-5725</span></strong></span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; vertical-align: middle;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;"><br />
12/31/2019</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; vertical-align: middle;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; vertical-align: middle;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; vertical-align: middle;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; vertical-align: middle;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">J  Ader</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; vertical-align: middle;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">MuckRock News DEPT MR 84770</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; vertical-align: middle;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">Somerville, MA 02144</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; vertical-align: middle;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; vertical-align: middle;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt 0.5in; text-align: justify; text-indent: -0.5in; vertical-align: middle;">&nbsp;</p>
<div style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; text-indent: -0.5in; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">Re:<span style="white-space: pre;">	</span>Public Records Request, dated&nbsp;12/29/2019&nbsp;File #W022214-122919 for Other Public Records</span></div>
<div style="text-align: left;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; text-indent: -0.5in; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><span style="white-space: pre;">	</span>Matter</span><span style="font-size: 10pt; text-indent: -0.5in; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">&nbsp;&ndash; Clarification of Request Needed</span></div>
<p style="margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px;">&nbsp;</p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; vertical-align: middle;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify; vertical-align: middle;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">&nbsp;</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">Dear&nbsp;J  Ader:</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 7.5pt;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;"><br />
</span></p>
<div style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: verdana;">On 12/29/2019, you submitted a public records request to the City of Kent wherein you sought records for:</span></div>
<div style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: verdana;"><em></em></span>
<p><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">All documents pertaining to Converus EyeDetect (https://converus.com). Documents being requested here should include - but are not limited to - the following:</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Invoices or receipts for the purchase of any EyeDetect product/service<br />
</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- MOUs from Converus</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Brochures or product/service specifications regarding EyeDetect</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Privacy policies regarding EyeDetect product/services</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Any/all manuals regarding EyeDetect product/services</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Guidelines mentioning EyeDetect product/services</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Bulletins mentioning EyeDetect product/services</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Briefings mentioning EyeDetect product/services</span></p>
<p><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Any/all digitally disseminated publications from your agency mentioning EyeDetect product/services</span></p>
</div>
<p style="margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">Your request for "all documents" <span style="text-align: justify;">pertaining to Converus EyeDetect&nbsp;</span>fails to identify public records and the City requires clarification from you before it can undertake reasonable search efforts.&nbsp;</span></p>
<div style="margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;"><span style="text-align: justify; font-family: Verdana;">The PRA only requires an agency to provide public records for inspection upon receipt of a &ldquo;request for identifiable public records.&rdquo; While the PRA does not require much from requestors, it does require that requestors first identify public records before any duty shifts to an agency to produce records. An &ldquo;identifiable public record&rdquo; is one in which the requestor has given a &ldquo;reasonable description enabling the government employee to locate the requested records.&rdquo;</span><a href="file:///C:/Users/TAlcorn/AppData/Local/Microsoft/Windows/Temporary%20Internet%20Files/Content.Outlook/5XEMIHG4/Watson-PRR21306_Clarifiction%20Request-11.04.2019.doc#_ftn1" name="_ftnref1" style="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="color: black;">[1]</span></a><span style="text-align: justify;"> The state Supreme Court has held that if a requesting party could meet the PRA&rsquo;s requirement of identifying the desired documents by requesting all of an agency&rsquo;s documents, the statute&rsquo;s identification requirement would be rendered meaningless.</span><a href="file:///C:/Users/TAlcorn/AppData/Local/Microsoft/Windows/Temporary%20Internet%20Files/Content.Outlook/5XEMIHG4/Watson-PRR21306_Clarifiction%20Request-11.04.2019.doc#_ftn2" name="_ftnref2" style="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="color: black;">[2]</span></a><span style="text-align: justify;"> For that reason, Washington courts have consistently held that an agency is excused from complying with a request that fails to identify public records.</span><a href="file:///C:/Users/TAlcorn/AppData/Local/Microsoft/Windows/Temporary%20Internet%20Files/Content.Outlook/5XEMIHG4/Watson-PRR21306_Clarifiction%20Request-11.04.2019.doc#_ftn3" name="_ftnref3" style="font-size: 10pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="color: black;">[3]</span></a><br />
</span></div>
<div style="margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px;">
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;"><span style="font-family: Verdana;">A request for &ldquo;information&rdquo; or a request for &ldquo;any and all&rdquo; records &ldquo;relating to&rdquo; a broad topic is not a request for an identifiable public record. While a requestor need not identify the exact record he seeks, a requestor must provide a meaningful description of the record that is helpful for the person charged with finding the record. However, the PRA does not require agencies to research public records, only to make identified public records available to the public.<a href="file:///C:/Users/TAlcorn/AppData/Local/Microsoft/Windows/Temporary%20Internet%20Files/Content.Outlook/5XEMIHG4/Watson-PRR21306_Clarifiction%20Request-11.04.2019.doc#_ftn4" name="_ftnref4"><span style="color: black;">[4]</span></a> Nor does the PRA allow unbridled searches of an agency&rsquo;s property&mdash;it only allows public access to </span><span style="font-family: Verdana;">government records once those records have first been identified in a public records request.<a href="file:///C:/Users/TAlcorn/AppData/Local/Microsoft/Windows/Temporary%20Internet%20Files/Content.Outlook/5XEMIHG4/Watson-PRR21306_Clarifiction%20Request-11.04.2019.doc#_ftn5" name="_ftnref5"><span style="color: black;">[5]</span></a> Finally, while RCW 42.56.080(2) provides an agency may not deny a request &ldquo;</span><span style="font-family: Verdana;">for <em><span style="text-decoration: underline;">identifiable </span></em>public records solely on the basis that the request is overbroad,&rdquo; this statutory requirement presupposes that a proper request for identifiable records has first been received by the agency. Such is not the case with your requests.</span><br />
</span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="color: black; font-size: 13px; font-family: Verdana;">The following identifiable records you have requested will be researched:</span></p>
<div style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Invoices or receipts for the purchase of any EyeDetect product/service&nbsp;</span></div>
<div>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- MOUs from Converus</span></p>
<div style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Brochures or product/service specifications regarding EyeDetect</span></div>
<div style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">&nbsp;</span></div>
<div style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Privacy policies regarding EyeDetect product/services</span></div>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Any/all manuals regarding EyeDetect product/services</span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Guidelines mentioning EyeDetect product/services</span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Bulletins mentioning EyeDetect product/services</span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">- Briefings mentioning EyeDetect product/services</span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">Your request for "Any/all digitally disseminated publications from your agency mentioning EyeDetect product/services" does require clarification.&nbsp; The City utilizes email as a medium for communication with it's employees digitally, in order to conduct a global email search, the following information will be required:</span></p>
<ul>
    <li style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">Date range</span></li>
    <li style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">Specific Email Search Terms&nbsp;</span></li>
    <li style="text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 13px;">If you are seeking additional records outside of email for this portion of your request, please identify those records as well.&nbsp;</span><span style="text-align: left;"></span></li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
<p style="text-align: justify; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">The City will begin compiling the identifiable records you requested; if additional clarification is required in that process, we will contact you as soon as possible.&nbsp; We currently anticipate records will be available to you in full or in an installment basis within 20 business days.&nbsp; </span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana;">We will&nbsp;</span><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 10pt;">wait for your clarification as described above before we can begin any form of a global email search.&nbsp; If you fail to clarify that portion your request within 30 calendar days from the date of this letter, the City will consider that portion of your request abandoned.</span></p>
<p style="text-align: justify; margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 10px;"><span style="font-family: Verdana; font-size: 10pt;">If you have any questions, please contact the City Clerk&rsquo;s Office at 253-856-5725.</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 7.5pt;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">Thank you.</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 7.5pt;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">Sincerely,</span></p>
<p style="margin-bottom: 7.5pt; line-height: normal;"><strong><span style="font-family: 'Segoe Script', sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">Tiffany Alcorn</span></strong><span style="font-size: 13.5pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;"></span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">Tiffany Alcorn</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 0.0001pt; text-align: justify;"><span style="font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 10pt;">Public Disclosure Administrator</span></p>
<p style="margin: 0in 0in 12pt; line-height: 15pt;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"></span></p>
<p class="HeaderDivisionPhone" style="margin: 0in 0in 0pt; font-family: Verdana; text-align: right;"><span style="font-size: 10pt;"><span style="text-align: start;"></span><strong><span style="line-height: 15.3333px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"></span><span style="text-align: start;">City of Kent Administration</span></strong><strong><span style="line-height: 15.3333px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"><br />
</span></strong><span style="line-height: 15.3333px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">Derek Matheson, CAO</span></span></p>
<div class="HeaderDivisionPhone" style="margin: 0in 0in 0pt; font-family: Verdana; text-align: right;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 15.3333px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">&nbsp;</span></div>
<div class="HeaderDivisionPhone" style="margin: 0in 0in 0pt; font-family: Verdana; text-align: right;"><span style="font-size: 10pt; line-height: 15.3333px; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;"></span><hr align="left" size="1" width="33%" />
<div id="ftn1">
<p style="text-align: justify;"><a href="file:///C:/Users/TAlcorn/AppData/Local/Microsoft/Windows/Temporary%20Internet%20Files/Content.Outlook/5XEMIHG4/Watson-PRR21306_Clarifiction%20Request-11.04.2019.doc#_ftnref1" name="_ftn1"><span style="font-size: 8pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman';">[1]</span></a><span style="font-size: 8pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">&nbsp;<em>Wood v. Lowe</em>, 102 Wn. App. 872, 498 (2000), citing&nbsp;<em>Bonamy v. Seattle</em>, 92 Wn. App. 403 (1998).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="ftn2">
<p style="text-align: justify;"><a href="file:///C:/Users/TAlcorn/AppData/Local/Microsoft/Windows/Temporary%20Internet%20Files/Content.Outlook/5XEMIHG4/Watson-PRR21306_Clarifiction%20Request-11.04.2019.doc#_ftnref2" name="_ftn2"><span style="font-size: 8pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman';">[2]</span></a><span style="font-size: 8pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">&nbsp;<em>Hangartner v. Seattle</em>, 151 Wn.2d 439, 448 (2004).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="ftn3">
<p style="text-align: justify;"><a href="file:///C:/Users/TAlcorn/AppData/Local/Microsoft/Windows/Temporary%20Internet%20Files/Content.Outlook/5XEMIHG4/Watson-PRR21306_Clarifiction%20Request-11.04.2019.doc#_ftnref3" name="_ftn3"><span style="font-size: 8pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman';">[3]</span></a><span style="font-size: 8pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">&nbsp;See, e.g.,&nbsp;<em>Hangartner v. Seattle</em>, 151 Wn.2d 439, 448-449 (2004);&nbsp;<em>Bonamy v. Seattle</em>, 92 Wn. App. 403, 410-412 (1998);&nbsp;<em>Wood v. Lowe</em>, 102 Wn. App. 872, 878&mdash;879 (2000);&nbsp;<em>Belenski v. Jefferson County</em>, 187 Wn. App. 724 (2015)</span></p>
</div>
<div id="ftn4">
<p style="text-align: justify;"><a href="file:///C:/Users/TAlcorn/AppData/Local/Microsoft/Windows/Temporary%20Internet%20Files/Content.Outlook/5XEMIHG4/Watson-PRR21306_Clarifiction%20Request-11.04.2019.doc#_ftnref4" name="_ftn4"><span style="font-size: 8pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman';">[4]</span></a><span style="font-size: 8pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">&nbsp;<em>Bomany v. Seattle</em>, 92 Wn. App. 403, 409 (1998).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="ftn5">
<p style="text-align: justify;"><a href="file:///C:/Users/TAlcorn/AppData/Local/Microsoft/Windows/Temporary%20Internet%20Files/Content.Outlook/5XEMIHG4/Watson-PRR21306_Clarifiction%20Request-11.04.2019.doc#_ftnref5" name="_ftn5"><span style="font-size: 8pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif; font-size: 8pt; font-family: 'Times New Roman';">[5]</span></a><span style="font-size: 8pt; font-family: Verdana, sans-serif;">&nbsp;<em>Hangartner v. Seattle</em>, 151 Wn.2d 439, 448 (2004).</span></p>
